You are an adversarial reviewer of scientific figures for a research proposal. The attached PNGs are rendered at 2x from SVG and will be displayed about 850 px wide. Try hard to find reasons each figure should not ship. For EACH image, by file order, report: (a) overlapping or colliding text, (b) lines or arrows that cross text or other arrows confusingly, (c) arrows whose direction or endpoints are ambiguous, (d) text too small to read at display size, (e) excess text that belongs in a caption, (f) the one main point and whether a reader gets it in 5 seconds, (g) concrete fixes with coordinates or element names. Then give a verdict per figure: ship / fix / redraw. Focus: Round 3 of proposal 06, 'Who does self-improvement leave behind?' (a self-improving agent loop that keeps edits lowering mean error can harm a pre-defined minority, the StaBLE fall-risk group). These seven figures changed after round 2. Points, in file order: (1) edit-effect-scatter: illustrative, with the tail weighted 0.125 the mean rule's acceptance line is nearly vertical, so under negative correlation many accepted edits harm the tail (orange); wording now 'accepted, tail harmed' in both places. (2) drift-sign-map: computed from the law, the threshold correlation rho* below which selection harms the tail depends on tail share and relative spread of tail effects; -0.143 at pi = 0.125 with equal spreads; region labels and legend rewritten in plain language; the noise statement is in the caption. (3) timing-regimes-geometry: schematic Fisher geometric model; inside the ball the expected tail gain per generation is negative; insets show cumulative tail gain since the seed; seeds 1 and 3 no longer collinear; descriptors moved to the caption. (4) guarantee-validity-and-price: preliminary simulation; left axis is now the observed rate of breaching the tail margin M with the event per method defined directly beneath; the green series are dodged 6 px at each n so markers stay separate (the caption gives exact values). (5) instrumented-loop: a 'saved checkpoints' arrow now feeds the sealed test box, and the forecast box names its target (the generation-50 tail change). (6) stable-person-splits: subtitle now 'stratified by fall-risk status'. (7) dose-response-design: bracket now 'model predicts zero drift near pi = 0.23' and the callout starts 'at pi = 0.40'. Judge each figure on its own; give ship unless a real defect remains.. Do not run commands or modify files.

